            <ArticleTitle>Smoking and narcotics use among chronic pain patients.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1253-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Among 137 noncancer patients having pain for more than 6 mo. and being within 30 to 69 yr. of age, narcotics users were evenly distributed but tobacco smokers were significantly more likely than nonsmokers to use narcotics.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
